\section{Primary BRMM source and bounded-bias motion theorem}
\label{sec:brmm-source}

BRMM (bounded recurrent marine motion) describes the physical wave-displacement
source for the practical-motion theorem. COMPLETE-BRMM includes the hard
oscillatory-generator condition below as well as the retained window and
execution premises. One physical root and continuation produce the IMU,
frontend, geometry, committed $\tau,\sigma_{aw},R_S,T_S$ and actual covariance
and event history. No independent acceleration, bias, tuner or
pseudo-measurement boxes are introduced.

\subsection{Wave coordinates and the hard physical generator}
\label{sec:brmm-physical-wave-generator}

Write the CoG translation in a fixed inertial frame as
\[
 x_{\rm CoG}(t)=x_{\rm eq}(t)+p_m(t),\qquad
 v_m=\dot p_m,\quad a_m=\dot v_m.
\]
Here $p_m$ is the oscillatory wave-induced displacement relative to the
local equilibrium, not absolute vessel position. A change of global position
origin changes $x_{\rm eq}$, not $p_m$. Current, propulsion, leeway, secular
wave drift and baseline translation belong to $x_{\rm eq}$. This separation
is not a license to change accelerometer truth: $\ddot x_{\rm eq}$ must be
zero, explicitly compensated, or retained in the declared same-history
sensor/model disturbance. An accelerating baseline is not silently removed
from the IMU. In a moving or rotating reference implementation, all additional
frame terms likewise need an explicit same-history model or disturbance bound.

\paragraph{Corrected COMPLETE-BRMM admission.}
In addition to the pointwise, window, attitude, bias and execution conditions
below, every complete physical continuation must have one of the following
hard generator certificates, with \emph{uniform, fixed family budgets}. The
same generator produces $p_m,v_m,a_m$; these are not free integration constants.
Quiet motion remains admitted. Neither a power spectrum, a significant wave
height, a finite replay nor an asymptotic zero-mean assertion replaces these
pathwise conditions. The executable contract is
\texttt{ou3\_brmm\_physical\_wave\_source.py}; a bare finite-window jet is no
longer sufficient for current COMPLETE-BRMM admission.

\paragraph{Spectral certificate.}
Let $A,B$ be finite real vector measures on $(0,\infty)$ and require
\begin{align}
 p_m(t)&=\int_{(0,\infty)}\cos(\omega t)\,dA(\omega)\nonumber\\
       &\quad+\int_{(0,\infty)}\sin(\omega t)\,dB(\omega),\nonumber\\
 M_j&=\int_{(0,\infty)}\omega^j\bigl(d|A|(\omega)+d|B|(\omega)\bigr)
       \le\overline M_j<\infty.
 \label{eq:brmm-hard-spectral-source}
\end{align}
Require these bounds for $j=-1,0,1,2$.
The total variations use the Euclidean vector norm. There is no zero-frequency
atom in the displacement. These are hard amplitude-measure bounds, not spectral
power moments. They cover finitely many harmonics and continuous amplitude
measures without replacing the frequency continuum by a grid. The coefficients
and phases are one complete history, not fresh choices at successive words.
A physical band $0<\omega_{\min}\le\omega\le\omega_{\max}<\infty$ and a hard
mass bound $\overline M_0$ suffice, with
$\overline M_{-1}\le\overline M_0/\omega_{\min}$ and
$\overline M_j\le\omega_{\max}^j\overline M_0$ for $j=1,2$.
A strict frequency cutoff is not necessary when the weighted inverse moment
itself is finite. The shipping tuner frequency limits are \emph{not} such a
physical cutoff. Derivatives of the same representation give $v_m,a_m$;
$\overline M_0,\overline M_1,\overline M_2$ bound their respective norms.

For the stationary vessel RAO model, a mode is
$\operatorname{Re}(H_i a_i e^{\mathrm i\varphi_i-\mathrm i\omega_i t})$.
Its real and imaginary vector coefficients provide $A_i,B_i$ in
Eq.~\eqref{eq:brmm-hard-spectral-source}; the fixed heading rotation preserves
Euclidean norms. Mean elevation and secular translation are not wave modes.
All admitted incident amplitudes, RAOs and frequencies must satisfy the hard
family bounds. The external RAO API can accept zero frequency, so API validity
alone does not establish this corrected physical admission.

\paragraph{Bounded shaping-state certificate.}
Alternatively, in fixed declared units let
\begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
 \dot x&=A_sx+B_su, &p_m&=C_sx+D_su,\\
 \phi_{\rm w}&=L_sx, &L_sA_s&=C_s,\quad L_sB_s=D_s.
 \end{aligned}
 \label{eq:brmm-potential-generator}
\end{equation}
Require a common positive definite $P_s$, a hard input norm $U$, an initial
radius $r_0$, and
\[
 A_s^\top P_s+P_sA_s\preceq-2\alpha P_s,\qquad
 \|u(t)\|\le U,\qquad \|x(0)\|_{P_s}\le r_0.
\]
For $\alpha>0$, set
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 b\ge\|P_s^{1/2}B_s\|_2,\qquad
 \ell\ge\|L_sP_s^{-1/2}\|_2,\\
 r=\max(r_0,bU/\alpha).
 \end{gathered}
\]
Then $\|x(t)\|_{P_s}\le r$. The lossless case $\alpha=0,B_s=0$ instead
uses $r=r_0$ and includes bounded harmonic oscillators. The executable exact
rational certificate uses the valid trace bounds
$b^2\ge\operatorname{tr}(B_s^\top P_sB_s)$ and
$\ell^2\ge\operatorname{tr}(L_sP_s^{-1}L_s^\top)$ with outward square roots.
It verifies the matrix inequalities and output identities, not asserted flags.
Admitted inputs must also give an absolutely continuous physical jet
$\dot p_m=v_m,\dot v_m=a_m$ with the declared motion caps. Bounded input alone
does not establish those derivative or sensor conditions.

A time-varying realization requires the stronger identity
$\dot L_s+L_sA_s=C_s$, $L_sB_s=D_s$, a uniform state/output bound, and its
actual invariant proof. At a mode or parameter switch the same potential,
physical jet and source ancestry must be transported continuously, with the
successor invariant established. These generalized identities specify an
extension obligation; the current numerical checker implements constant
matrices only. Bounded per-window parameter rates do not prove an indefinite
primitive bound. For example,
$(1+\varepsilon\cos t)\cos t$ has a carrier frequency one and bounded
amplitude/rates but contains the DC term $\varepsilon/2$. Arbitrary independent
word restarts can similarly accumulate a nonzero displacement integral.

\begin{lemma}[Hard all-time centered displacement primitive]
\label{lem:brmm-derived-centered-primitive}
For a fixed qualified family in Eq.~\eqref{eq:brmm-hard-spectral-source}, take
$D_S=2\overline M_{-1}$. For Eq.~\eqref{eq:brmm-potential-generator}, take
$D_S=2\ell r$. Then every admitted history satisfies, for all relevant $t,u$,
\begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
 S_m(t)-S_m(u)&=\int_u^t p_m(s)\,ds\\
              &=\phi_{\rm w}(t)-\phi_{\rm w}(u),\\
 \|S_m(t)-S_m(u)\|&\le D_S.
 \end{aligned}
 \label{eq:brmm-derived-primitive}
\end{equation}
In particular, for the actual Live time $t_L$, the one-time coordinate
$S_L(t)=S_m(t)-S_m(t_L)$ has $S_L(t_L)=0$ and $\|S_L(t)\|\le D_S$.
No absolute $S_m$ origin is bounded, no position is re-anchored, and no later
word resets $S_L$ or the retained $\phi_{\rm w}(t_L)$.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
In the spectral case define
\[
 \phi_{\rm w}(t)=\int_{(0,\infty)}
       \frac{\sin(\omega t)\,dA(\omega)-\cos(\omega t)\,dB(\omega)}{\omega}.
\]
The inverse-moment bound gives $\|\phi_{\rm w}(t)\|\le\overline M_{-1}$ uniformly.
The $M_0$ bound justifies differentiation under the integral, giving
$\dot\phi_{\rm w}=p_m$. In the shaping case the two exact output identities give
$\dot\phi_{\rm w}=p_m$. For $y=\|x\|_{P_s}$ the upper Dini derivative obeys
$D^+y\le-\alpha y+bU$; comparison gives $y\le r$. When $B_s=0$ and
$\alpha=0$, the energy is nonincreasing. Thus $\|\phi_{\rm w}(t)\|\le\ell r$.
The fundamental theorem of calculus and the triangle inequality prove
Eq.~\eqref{eq:brmm-derived-primitive}. Compatible switches preserve the same
potential and telescope; a newly chosen independent potential offset would
invalidate that argument.
\end{proof}
For finitely many fixed harmonics this specializes to
$D_S=2\sum_i(\|A_i\|+\|B_i\|)/\omega_i$. If $p_m(t)\equiv d\ne0$
indefinitely, its primitive has norm $(t-u)\|d\|$, contradicting the lemma.
Finite flat segments are not excluded; only indefinite nonzero displacement
DC is excluded by the generator theorem. Zero wave motion is still admitted.

The existing $300\,\mathrm{m\,s}$ number is an error working/retention search
radius, not a physical amplitude premise. It neither sets nor caps $D_S$.
For example, the zero-DC heave family $p_z(t)=\cos(t/n)$, $n\ge10$,
has uniformly bounded displacement, speed and acceleration, yet its exact
primitive diameter is $2n$. Its normalized gravity-direction disturbance is
zero when the vertical acceleration cannot reverse specific force. Thus
positive individual frequencies and the old pointwise caps do not supply a
uniform bound for that family. This is a numerical-family qualification gap,
not a counterexample to the corrected fixed-budget theorem or to the filter.
The current broad source declaration does not supply a qualified numerical
$\overline M_{-1}$ or common shaping-state envelope. Consequently a numerical
physical $D_S$, its comparison with that working radius, and full physical
source qualification remain open. A derived bound above 300 must not be
clipped; nor does an upper bound alone prove an attained maximum or an
infeasible error tube. Those questions require the retained physical/error
graph and actual first-exit calculation.

\subsection{BRMM physical motion: no acceleration DC in either branch}

Let $a_m(t)\in\mathbb R^3$ be non-gravitational CoG acceleration in one
fixed physical world frame. On the admitted Normal-Live execution require
\[
 \|a_m(t)\|\le8.0\ {\rm m\,s^{-2}},\qquad
 \|\omega(t)\|\le30^\circ/{\rm s}.
\]
Thus $1.80665\le\|a_m-g\|\le17.80665\ {\rm m\,s^{-2}}$ for standard
gravity. Positive sea-height cases satisfy $0<H_s\le8.5\ {\rm m}$;
zero motion is also admitted. At $H_s=0$ use fixed physical coordinate
scales, never division by sea height. These caps are admission premises,
not assertions that every reference replay satisfies them. The widened
acceleration cap retains the separate same-history normalized gravity-direction
qualification used by the private Mahony proof:
$r(t)=m(t)+\dot\xi(t)$ with $\|m(t)\|\le0.05$ and
$\|\xi(t)\|\le1.0\,\mathrm s$. The same $r$ is the actual normalized
direction forcing, not an independently chosen vector. Oscillatory acceleration
alone does not prohibit rectification in its normalized direction.

\paragraph{BRMM-0: prohibit physical acceleration DC.}
For the entire admitted continuation, require an absolutely continuous
same-history velocity primitive $v_m$ and a uniform finite constant $V_m$:
\begin{equation}
 a_m=\dot v_m\quad\hbox{a.e.},\qquad
 \sup_{t\ge t_{\rm Live}}\|v_m(t)\|\le V_m<\infty.
 \label{eq:brmm-zero-dc}
\end{equation}
This applies to both Q and O and every transition between them. For every
$t$ and $T>0$ within that continuation, the fundamental theorem of calculus gives
\begin{equation}
 \left\|\frac1T\int_t^{t+T}a_m(s)\,ds\right\|
 \le\frac{2V_m}{T}\longrightarrow0
 \quad\hbox{uniformly in }t.
 \label{eq:brmm-zero-mean}
\end{equation}
In particular, $a_m(t)\equiv d\ne0$ is prohibited: its primitive grows as
$td$. A persistent nonzero long-time mean hidden inside oscillatory
acceleration is also prohibited. Finite transient impulses and zero motion
remain admissible. A fixed-window bound alone, however small, does not
exclude all constant accelerations; nor does small AC energy.

For example, a finite harmonic acceleration with fixed vector coefficients
and frequencies $\omega_i>0$,
\begin{equation}
 a_m(t)=\sum_i\bigl[A_i\cos(\omega_i t)+B_i\sin(\omega_i t)\bigr],
\end{equation}
has the same-history primitive
\begin{equation}
 v_m(t)=v_0+\sum_i\frac{A_i\sin(\omega_i t)-B_i\cos(\omega_i t)}{\omega_i}.
\end{equation}
It satisfies BRMM-0 for all time with
$V_m=\|v_0\|+\sum_i(\|A_i\|+\|B_i\|)/\omega_i$.
A constant velocity term contributes no acceleration DC, but is not a wave
velocity unless its displacement and generator also satisfy the corrected
source conditions. Baseline drift belongs to $x_{\rm eq}$. Uniformity over a family requires a uniform bound on this expression.
This analytical implication does not by itself certify a replay's exact
physical attachment, the acceleration/rate caps, or O-branch return lobes.

Constant measurement offset belongs to BIAS0, not to $a_m$. Subtracting a
sample mean cannot manufacture physical BRMM membership: the same actual
acceleration must drive the source and observer. Sensor bias, compensation
residuals and model mismatch retain their own input budgets. Bounded
velocity alone does not bound displacement or the $S$ primitive. The corrected generator condition and
Lemma~\ref{lem:brmm-derived-centered-primitive} supply the missing displacement
primitive structure; its family budgets still require hard qualification. The actual $S=0$ residual
$\delta S-S_{\rm true}$ and its applied anisotropic $R_S$ remain in the graph.

\subsection{Window recurrence and quiet motion}

For every start time $t_k$ and common duration $T_R>0$, put
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 \bar a_k&=T_R^{-1}\int_{t_k}^{t_k+T_R}a_m(t)\,dt,\\
 E_k&=\int_{t_k}^{t_k+T_R}\|a_m(t)-\bar a_k\|^2\,dt.
 \end{aligned}
\]
Require the finite-window mean-reversion bound on \emph{both} branches,
\begin{equation}
 \left\|\int_{t_k}^{t_k+T_R}a_m(t)\,dt\right\|\le V_R.
 \label{eq:brmm-window-impulse}
\end{equation}
One may take $V_R=2V_m$ from BRMM-0; a smaller bound needs separate evidence.
Every window satisfies one of
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 {\rm Q}:&\quad E_k\le E_q,\\
 {\rm O}:&\quad E_k>E_q,\quad E_k\ge E_{\min},\\
 &\quad E_q\ge0,\quad E_{\min}>0.
 \end{aligned}
\]
Only O additionally requires disjoint subintervals $I_k^+,I_k^-$ with
impulses $j_k^\pm=\int_{I_k^\pm}a_m(t)\,dt$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \|j_k^\pm\|\ge J_{\min}>0,\qquad
 (j_k^+)^\top j_k^-\le-\chi J_{\min}^2,\qquad\chi>0.
 \label{eq:brmm-opposing-lobes}
\end{equation}
No minimum wave amplitude or O-branch excitation is imposed on Q. Quiet
does not mean DC: Q still obeys BRMM-0, the corrected physical generator
condition and Eq.~\eqref{eq:brmm-window-impulse}. An optional bound
$\mathrm{TV}_{[t_k,t_k+T_R]}(a_m)\le V_a$ may be added if a concrete
finite-map enclosure needs it; it is not currently a frozen premise.

The initial audit uses $T_R=10\,{\rm s}$, quiet RMS thresholds
$0.03$ and $0.05\,{\rm m\,s^{-2}}$ (respectively
$E_q=0.009$ and $0.025\,{\rm m^2\,s^{-3}}$), and candidate
$V_R=2\,{\rm m\,s^{-1}}$. These are diagnostic choices, not qualified
uniform constants. $T_R,E_q,V_R,E_{\min},J_{\min},\chi,V_a$ and the primitive
bounds remain to be assigned with evidence.
The proposed outer tuner interval $[0.02,1.2]\,{\rm Hz}$ does not change the
shipping defaults $[0.03,1.2]\,{\rm Hz}$ and is not a physical motion
bandlimit. A $0.02\,{\rm Hz}$ sinusoid has a $50\,{\rm s}$ period:
opposing lobes in every $10\,{\rm s}$ window are not automatic.

\paragraph{Certificate entry and audit limits.}
The eight v1.2.1 vessel-response JONSWAP/PM--Stokes records at
$H_s\in\{0.27,1.5,4,8.5\}\,{\rm m}$ are tested on every sample-aligned
$10\,{\rm s}$ window. Outward arithmetic encloses binary64 sample values
under an explicit zero-order-hold interpretation. Stored lobe intervals
certify positive witnesses; a finite search finding none leaves the window
unresolved. Finite sampled statistics neither prove infinite-time BRMM-0
nor enclose physical intersample motion, all continuous window offsets,
Normal-Live entry, or the complete source family. They suggest candidate
constants and expose sampled-envelope violations; they do not set theorem constants.

The retained historical sampled v1.2.1 audit, evaluated against the former
$4\,\mathrm{m/s^2}$ acceleration cap (not the current 8 cap), contains 1,920,000 samples and 1,904,008 complete
sample-aligned windows. All windows fall in the diagnostic O branch.
There are 10,205 samples above the acceleration cap and 31,937 above
the rate cap. Restricting to the runtime Live flag leaves 10,002 and
31,589 such samples. Moreover, the runtime covariance settings differ
from the configured vector-covariance premises used by the conditional
matrix certificate. No sampled execution satisfies all audited admission
checks, even where the physical caps hold. The trace observer is bitwise
transparent to ordinary replay output; two of eight replays fail their
unchanged performance gates. None of these finite-record observations
promotes source admission, P4 or P5.

\paragraph{Proof obligations under the replacement source.}
BIAS0/1 supplies qualified true-bias bounds and its connected history;
estimate projection supplies compactness, not bias-error decay.
P1/P2 must attach each BRMM history to the exact shipping Normal-Live graph
(lever arm disabled, vibration guard transparent, all valid accelerometer
samples accepted, all asynchronous vector events, process floors, resets
and every due actual-$R_S$ correction). P3 retains $\delta=10^{-18}$ and its
matrix implications only where their actual premises are established.
Scalar BRMM recurrence does not prove vector persistent excitation,
especially in Q. The conditional P3 implication below covers Q, O and their
mixtures through the same execution premises in both modes. A source
declaration or sampled audit does not establish those premises.

\paragraph{What Normal-Live means for P3.}
It is an execution regime, not merely the runtime \texttt{Live} flag.
Write $\mathcal C_W$ for the existing explicit hypotheses used by the
matrix certificates: the source-generated Live covariance and shipping
held-to-active release; accepted accelerometer updates at every valid IMU
sample; the declared asynchronous vector-PE occurrences with one-second
recurrence, magnetic norm $10$--$200\,\mu{\rm T}$, vector sine separation at
least $0.1$, the stated specific-force bounds and body-rate cap; committed
OU and scheduler invariants; full configured process and measurement
covariances, PSD latent-acceleration floors, every due actual-$R_S$ update,
and each immediate covariance reset. The lever arm is disabled, the
vibration guard is dormant/transparent, required factorizations succeed,
and hard attitude rewrites are separate hybrid entries. Geometry bounds
must describe the actual Jacobians on that same history.

Some parts of $\mathcal C_W$ are shipping identities or clamp invariants;
accepted-vector recurrence, geometry and branch retention are execution
assumptions requiring separate admission evidence. Scalar BRMM recurrence
and the runtime Live flag do not imply them. In particular, no inequality
$\Omega_W\succeq\delta P_W$, nonlinear contraction, or bias-error decay is
assumed in $\mathcal C_W$.

The conditional P3 claim is
\[
 (\mathrm{BRMM}\ \text{and}\ \mathcal C_W)
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 \Omega_W-10^{-18}P_W\succeq0 .
\]
Its numerical chain uses the complete H18 information word and following
prediction, outward full-matrix prior-free completion, then the exact
held-to-active covariance bridge and event preservation. Those matrix
steps use no spectral membership or positive lower bound on wave energy.
Thus the same implication applies to Q, O and mixed histories satisfying
$\mathcal C_W$; this is not a claim that all BRMM histories satisfy it.
Physical source admission and P4 are separate.

The shipping bias projection changes the nominal bias but does not modify
$P$. The $P,\Psi,\Omega$ covariance comparison is consequently unchanged
by that event, including at the closed $0.4\,{\rm m\,s^{-2}}$ boundary.
Here $\Psi$ denotes the formal covariance-word transport, not the
derivative of the projected nonlinear error map.
Subsequent Jacobians and events must still satisfy $\mathcal C_W$. This
covariance identity neither bounds the nonlinear projection/reset error
map nor proves subsequent domain retention. The finite configured bias
correlation used in the A21 covariance bridge is not a conclusion that
physical bias error decays.

For P4, primitive and recurrence constraints enter the same full-history
graph and source/forcing forms in Eq.~\eqref{eq:brmm-motion-master}.
Where BIAS2 sharpens a gain, its positive sector must be proved on this
actual graph, not inferred from oscillatory source energy or bias compactness.
First check the attached finite-word motion master with useful channel gains.
Only a feasible quantitative endpoint and retention margin justifies outward
source coverage. Then certify every-prefix finite gain and first-exit
retention, including the closed projection boundary, before P5 capture.
Neither a sampled recurrence audit nor an unusably large finite input gain
promotes P4.

\subsection{Primary target: joint storage and practical motion stability}
\label{sec:brmm-bounded-bias-motion}

Use the finite motion error and physical accelerometer-bias coordinates
\begin{equation}
 \begin{aligned}
 e_H&=(c,\delta b_g,\delta v,\delta p,\delta S_L,\delta a_w)\in\mathbb R^{18},\\
 e_b&=b_a^{\rm true}-\hat b_a,\\
 z_J&=(e_H,e_b,b_a^{\rm true})\in\mathbb R^{24}.
 \end{aligned}
 \label{eq:brmm-motion-coordinates}
\end{equation}
Here $c$ is the finite Cayley coordinate, not a small-angle substitution.
H18 is the held-bias restriction of this joint physical/error graph; holding
an estimate does not freeze the physical BIAS0, BIAS1 or BIAS2 driver. A21
uses the actual active prediction/correction/projection map. In fixed physical
units the candidate compatible storage has the form
\begin{equation}
 \begin{gathered}
 W_J(z_J,\zeta)=z_J^\top M_J(\zeta)z_J,\\
 m_-\|z_J\|^2\le W_J\le m_+\|z_J\|^2,\\
 0<m_-\le m_+<\infty.
 \end{gathered}
 \label{eq:brmm-motion-storage}
\end{equation}
Coercivity on the held-mode restricted graph is understood using its legal
embedding. The source index $\zeta$ retains the physical generator and its
one Live potential, the true-bias ancestry, nominal state, full covariance,
frontend/statistics, candidate/active tuner and scheduler state. Motion/bias
cross information is retained. An A21 18-state marginal motion metric is
not substituted for this joint storage. The current information-metric and
joint-storage constructions are candidates requiring the compatible endpoint
and prefix tests below, not completed contraction certificates.

\begin{lemma}[Conditional compactness of accelerometer-bias error]
\label{lem:brmm-bias-compactness}
If $\|\hat b_a(0)\|\le R_b=0.4\,\mathrm{m/s^2}$ and the actual hold,
contractive bias prediction, norm-preserving frame transport and immediate
post-injection radial projection are executed, then $\|\hat b_a\|\le R_b$
at committed boundaries. For each separately admitted BIAS0/BIAS1/BIAS2
history with hard bound $\|b_a^{\rm true}\|\le B_{\rm true}$,
\begin{equation}
 \|e_b\|\le B_e:=B_{\rm true}+R_b.
 \label{eq:brmm-bias-compact-error}
\end{equation}
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Induction over the listed operations preserves the estimate ball. The
triangle inequality gives the error bound, without requiring true bias to
belong to the projection ball or converge to zero.
\end{proof}
The pre-projection correction is a separate auxiliary prefix and need not be
inside the committed ball. Every active/inactive projection branch, including
the closed boundary, remains in the exact graph. Stochastic bias spectra alone
do not provide the required deterministic true-bias envelope. Positive BIAS2
separation is optional, not a prerequisite for this bounded-bias objective.

For each complete same-history word require, in both modes and every admitted
Q/O continuation and bias family,
\begin{align}
 W_{J,k}^{\rm end}&\le\rho W_{J,k}^{\rm start}+C,
             &&0\le\rho<1,\label{eq:brmm-motion-endpoint}\\
 W_{J,k;\ell}&\le\Gamma W_{J,k}^{\rm start}+C_p,
             &&\ell\in\operatorname{Pref}(W_k),\quad \Gamma<\infty.
 \label{eq:brmm-motion-prefix}
\end{align}
The finite nonnegative budgets $C,C_p$ are derived from the physical generator,
each true-bias recurrence, sensor/model disturbances and the declared arithmetic
postcondition. The wave primitive is the retained $\phi_{\rm w}-\phi_{{\rm w},L}$ coordinate,
not an independent bounded disturbance port. Its exact $p/v/a$ recurrence and
signed source cross terms enter the supplies. Noise-free wave truth need not
obey the estimator's OU acceleration law, so its model-defect supply does not
vanish merely because measurement noise is zero.

For one augmented same-history graph coordinate $\xi$, write
$z_{J,0}=C_0\xi$, $z_{J,N}=C_N\xi$, and the joint physical/noise supply as
$\xi^\top Q\xi$. The endpoint master is
\begin{equation}
 L_J=C_N^\top M_{J,N}C_N-\rho C_0^\top M_{J,0}C_0-Q.
 \label{eq:brmm-motion-master}
\end{equation}
For valid sectors $\xi^\top\Pi_i\xi\ge0$ and $\lambda_i\ge0$, an outward
certificate of $-(L_J+\sum_i\lambda_i\Pi_i)\succeq0$ suffices. Redundant
coordinates may be eliminated only by exact graph identities; a strict
LDLT margin on the resulting nonredundant form is one implementation.
The prefix masters use their own exact event maps and valid prefix sectors.
No independent reconstruction of $P,H,R,K$, no independent choices of
$f,\sigma,\tau,T_S,R_S$, and no discarded motion/true-bias cross terms are
permitted. The same physical IMU history must generate WPE, band/statistics,
candidate/active EMA, staged commit, scheduler, Riccati, Joseph, reset and
projection successors. Source-uniform coverage is over those dependent
transitions, not a finite trajectory list.

Every completed literal event is a prefix: prediction, latent-acceleration
covariance floor, due S Joseph correction, accepted or rejected accelerometer
and magnetometer branches, finite attitude reset, active/inactive bias
projection, tuner/scheduler/not-due decisions, and allowed hybrid release or
reinitialization. A bound at sample boundaries does not certify intervening
charts or factorizations. The source potential at one word's exit is the next
word's entrance; $S_L$ is never reset between words.

Consecutive metrics must satisfy an explicit transport inequality
\[
 W_{J,k+1}^{\rm start}\le\mu W_{J,k}^{\rm end},\qquad
 \bar\rho=\mu\rho<1,\quad \bar C=\mu C.
\]
All hybrid affine forcing is charged before this comparison. A genuinely
identical shared covariance/storage at a common boundary gives $\mu=1$;
independently optimized metrics do not. Uniform coercivity, H18-to-A21
embedding, full covariance, physical bias, source and scheduler transport are
required at release and every other allowed hybrid. A metric jump cannot be
hidden in a claimed endpoint rate.

\begin{theorem}[Conditional indefinite practical stability and startup composition]
\label{thm:brmm-bounded-bias-motion}
Fix a corrected COMPLETE-BRMM family satisfying
Section~\ref{sec:brmm-physical-wave-generator}, including fixed uniform hard
budgets, the actual physical jet and baseline treatment. Admit BIAS0/1/2
separately and fix the hard sensor/model and finite-precision disturbance
budgets. Suppose source-uniform certificates establish the actual execution
premises $\mathcal C_W$, canonical P3 at $\delta=10^{-18}$, compatible coercive
joint storage, Eqs.~\eqref{eq:brmm-motion-endpoint}--\eqref{eq:brmm-motion-prefix},
and the non-energy source/state/covariance domains at every literal prefix.
Suppose a level $L$ and a chart-valid working level $L_{\rm chart}$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
 W_{J,k_c}^{\rm start}\le L,\qquad
 \bar\rho L+\bar C\le L,\qquad
 \Gamma L+C_p<L_{\rm chart}.
 \label{eq:brmm-motion-retention}
\end{equation}
The graph certificates must hold up to a possible first exit, not assume the
retention they are intended to prove. Then all successive compatible words
remain in their required domains and
\begin{align}
 W_{J,k_c+m}^{\rm start}
   &\le\bar\rho^m W_{J,k_c}^{\rm start}
       +\frac{1-\bar\rho^m}{1-\bar\rho}\bar C,\nonumber\\
 \limsup W_J&\le\Gamma\frac{\bar C}{1-\bar\rho}+C_p,
 \qquad \|e_b\|\le B_e.
 \label{eq:brmm-motion-ultimate}
\end{align}
In particular the 18 motion errors have the corresponding regional practical
ISS estimate by coercivity and the declared disturbance-dependent supplies.
For an end-to-end theorem, additionally certify that the actual Mahony/proxy
and startup-learning implementation reaches Live/H18 in finite time, that its
early-H18 trajectory reaches this basin in finite additional time, and that
the deployed magnetic-refinement guard and timing produce only the certified
H18-to-A21 transitions. Cover measured-period takeover and prior-frequency
timeout paths alike. Subject to those additional certificates, the preceding
indefinite conclusion holds from the actual startup, for every successive
admitted physical and bias continuation.
\end{theorem}
\begin{proof}
Metric compatibility converts each endpoint inequality to
$W_{k+1}^{\rm start}\le\bar\rho W_k^{\rm start}+\bar C$. Induction gives the
geometric sum and the first level inequality. The prefix inequality, its
strict chart margin and the separately certified non-energy domains exclude
a first exit. This validates every next application without assuming the
conclusion. Apply the prefix estimate to the geometric sum and take its
limsup. Coercivity bounds the motion output, and the bias lemma gives the
separate compactness statement. Finite startup and capture, followed by the
certified hybrid transports, compose with this invariant continuation.
\end{proof}

This is an explicit conditional theorem, not a report that its computational
premises have closed. The retained qualified runtime Live/H18 handoff bound
of 150 s is not a P4 capture bound. Numerical physical generator qualification,
complete same-history coverage, outward endpoint/every-prefix margins,
first-exit retention, the maximal certified basin, finite H18 capture and
post-release basin landing remain unclosed. P4 and P5 remain fail-closed.
A covariance ellipsoid is not automatically a hard error entry set; working
levels may be larger than fresh entry. No physical source constant may be
chosen by searching for a convenient passing error tube.

\paragraph{Shared integral-origin reduction at the fresh handoff.}
\label{sec:brmm-shared-S-origin}
Let $c=S_m(t_L)$ and define, once for the entire Live continuation,
$S_L(t)=S_m(t)-c$ and $e_{S,L}(t)=e_S(t)-c$.
This changes a proof reference, not a shipping state, sensor sample,
physical motion, or regularizer. At fresh entry $S_L(t_L)=e_{S,L}(t_L)=0$,
while $p_m(t_L)$ and $v_m(t_L)$ retain their same-source values.
For the actual zero-integral measurement,
\[
 r_S=-\hat S=e_S-S_m=e_{S,L}-S_L.
\]
Consequently the entire finite shipping event map is invariant to the common
translation $(S_m,e_S)\mapsto(S_m+c,e_S+c)$. In the signed error/source
ledger, with $E_S$ selecting the three integral coordinates, this is the
coefficientwise identity
\[
 (I-KH_S)E_S+K=E_S.
\]
It holds for the actual same-event $K$, without an independent gain box.
Prediction has $FE_S=E_S$; accelerometer and magnetometer geometries have
$HE_S=0$. Every residual, finite quaternion correction, reset transport,
radial bias projection, covariance update and scheduling decision is unchanged.
Thus the common-origin column remains $E_S$ at every literal prefix and is
zero after the reference row operation $e_{S,L}=e_S-c$. Since the origin
is not supplied to the executable, its binary32 trajectory is identical;
this cancellation adds no arithmetic error channel. Other arithmetic
qualification obligations are not discharged by this identity.

No independent $300\,\mathrm{m\,s}$ integral-error entrance ball represents
this graph. The earlier product may be used only as a conditional diagnostic
or a candidate working-domain scale. Removing a dependent entrance column
is not removing the three integral-error states from the retained 18-state
motion metric, and does not permit re-zeroing at successive word boundaries.
For $h\geq0$ the same physical continuation obeys
\[
 S_L(t_L+h)=h p_m(t_L)+\tfrac12h^2v_m(t_L)
       +\int_0^h\tfrac12(h-s)^2a_m(t_L+s)\,ds.
\]
Working/prefix bounds must retain this graph and its Joseph residual. For
admitted uniform primitive bounds, a consequence is
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 b(h)&=h\|p_m(t_L)\|+\tfrac12h^2\|v_m(t_L)\|+\tfrac16 A_mh^3,\\
 \|S_L(t_L+h)\|&\leq\min\{hP_m,b(h),D_S\}.
 \end{aligned}
\]
Any source-energy charge must also transform with its signed cross term:
$\int\|S_m-c\|^2=\int\|S_m\|^2-2c^\top\int S_m+T\|c\|^2$.
The original-reference error bound is recovered by
$\|e_S\|\leq\|e_{S,L}\|+\|c\|$; a uniform original-reference ultimate
bound therefore still requires an admitted uniform origin bound. Reanchoring
position is not the same harmless constant translation: it introduces the
secular term $-h p_m(t_L)$ into the integral reference and cannot be used to
assert $e_p(t_L)=0$ while retaining an indefinite bounded-primitive premise.

This exact reduction proves neither a common compatible metric nor endpoint
contraction. Those still require a source-uniform reachable entry and
continuation cover, coercivity, endpoint and literal-every-prefix outward
augmented LDLT, all retained domains, and finite-precision ISS charges. The
frozen-map values $4.5788$ and $0.9411/0.6537$ diagnose the old independent
entry factor, not an admissible nonlinear chart exit or a closed P4 theorem.
P4 and finite-time startup capture remain unclosed until these obligations
are certified for prior/measured adaptation, all BIAS families, and every
allowed hybrid transition.


\paragraph{Historical obstruction under the old finite-window-only source.}
\label{sec:brmm-indefinite-S-obstruction}
The old finite-window primitive qualification fixed
$V_m=5\,\mathrm{m/s}$ and $P_m=7.361215932167728\,\mathrm m$ and retained
$\dot S_m=p_m$ with short-window increment bounds, but did not bind $p_m$
to a bounded oscillatory generator potential. The following exact result is
retained as a regression for that old definition only. Its witness is not
admitted by current corrected COMPLETE-BRMM.

\begin{lemma}[Quiet-source ambiguity and finite all-18 bounds]
\label{prop:brmm-indefinite-S-obstruction}
Suppose the physical source admits both histories
$p_m^\pm(t)=\pm d$, $v_m^\pm=a_m^\pm=\omega^\pm=0$, $R^\pm=I$, for a
fixed $0<\|d\|<P_m$, with the same sensor records, configuration and
initial executable state. No deterministic sensor-only execution can give
both histories an eventually finite centered integral-error bound. In
particular they cannot both enter, in finite time, a finite working tube
for an all-18 storage satisfying Eq.~\eqref{eq:brmm-motion-storage} and
remain there indefinitely.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
The two physical histories satisfy the finite-window primitive equations,
all pointwise motion caps, zero acceleration DC, every Q energy/impulse
inequality, and the gravity-direction forcing qualification. Take zero
sensor noise and fixed magnetic field $(20,0,40)\,\mu\mathrm T$. Its
squared norm is $2000$ and squared sine separation from gravity is $1/5$;
these physical vector properties do not assert acceptance of every future
executable event. Zero physical bias belongs separately to each family:
set every BIAS0 component to zero, the BIAS1 root/amplitude/deterministic
component to zero, or the BIAS2 bounded-variation drift to zero. Each own
recurrence then gives $0=\phi_{\rm true}0+0$, including BIAS2's factor one.

Position and its integral are not inputs to the shipping IMU/magnetic
wrapper. The sensor histories are identical, so all private observers,
WPE/statistics, candidate/active/staged tuner states, scheduler states,
reachable covariances, geometries, measurement covariances, gains and
branch decisions are identical by induction over the actual completed
events. This is an equality of entire executions, not independent choices
of $P,H,R,K$ or $f,\sigma,\tau,T_S,R_S$. If that common execution fails an
indefinite required domain or is undefined, the requested conclusion has
already failed. Otherwise it has the same $t_L$ and nominal $\hat S$.

Apply the established origin reduction separately at that common handoff.
For $h=t-t_L\ge0$,
\[
 S_L^\pm(t_L+h)=\pm h d,\qquad
 e_{S,L}^\pm(t_L+h)=\pm h d-\hat S(t_L+h).
\]
Both centered errors are zero at fresh entry. At every later completed
event,
\begin{equation}
 e_{S,L}^+-e_{S,L}^-=2h d,\qquad
 \max\{\|e_{S,L}^+\|,\|e_{S,L}^-\|\}\ge h\|d\|.
 \label{eq:brmm-S-ambiguity-lower}
\end{equation}
In a shared source/error graph the position column is
$B(h)=E_p+hE_S$. Physical prediction sends it to $B(h+\Delta t)$.
For S Joseph events, $H_SB(h)-hI=0$; vector events have $HB(h)=0$.
Consequently every actual correction has the same residual for the two
histories. Finite reset/projection, covariance floors, H18-to-A21 release,
late north/tilt reinitialization and not-due/rejected branches act on the
same executable state and preserve the difference. No small-angle or
linearized reset argument is needed. Identical binary32 inputs and state
also give identical rounding; the physical source column is not rounded
into the executable. Deployment arithmetic qualification is not claimed.

If both histories had finite eventual bounds, choose $h$ larger than
both finite capture times and the sum of those bounds divided by
$2\|d\|$. Equation~\eqref{eq:brmm-S-ambiguity-lower} is a contradiction.
At least one \emph{fixed} history therefore has unbounded limsup. Different
source-dependent metrics do not help: uniform coercivity implies
$\max(W_+,W_-)\ge m_-h^2\|d\|^2$ in fixed units. The same statement holds
with the corresponding fixed S-coordinate scale. It cannot be absorbed
by compatible metric transport into a finite invariant storage level.
\end{proof}

For $\|d\|=1/8\,\mathrm m$, every 3 s increment is only
$3/8\,\mathrm{m\,s}$, yet at least one of the pair exceeds a
$300\,\mathrm{m\,s}$ \emph{working} integral-error radius when
$h>2400\,\mathrm s$. This is not an independent S entrance ball or a
claim of attitude/Cayley chart escape. The continuous physical-S energy is
\[
 \int_h^{h+3}\|s d\|^2\,ds
   =\|d\|^2(3h^2+9h+9),
\]
which also illustrates why a bounded increment cannot be substituted for
an indefinite absolute-source budget. This illustrative energy does not
replace the actual signed discrete ISS port cost. A conditional ISS
inequality with an unbounded physical-S input may still hold; it does not
yield the requested finite ultimate bound or first-exit constants.

This is classification B for the old finite-window-only infinite target,
and a source-specification omission E relative to the intended wave semantics.
It is not an established unstable nominal trajectory or a failure of P3.
Lemma~\ref{lem:brmm-derived-centered-primitive} now excludes the indefinite
nonzero-position witness by its physical generator theorem. The executable
regression retains the exact old paired-history proof and separately checks
\nolinkurl{constant_nonzero_position_zero_velocity_history_admitted=false}
under the corrected source. No nominal filter change or repeated origin reset
is made. Sign symmetry alone does not make general oscillatory $p$ and $-p$
histories sensor-indistinguishable, so the old DC argument supplies no general
$D_S\le300$ physical ceiling. The remaining numerical physical-family
qualification is E, and the nonlinear coverage, endpoint/prefix, retention
and capture obligations remain separate.
